                <pb facs="0385" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.00/1165.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Commissioner to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Puerto Cortes</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March 7,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Dawson says Bertrand was elected first designate by Congress on this date;
                    that the Vice President was expected to arrive at the capital the following day;
                    and that many of the Government forces were retiring for the purpose of
                    disarmament. Adds that he will arrive in Washington March 19.</p>
            </div>
